From ede7c0e1e25642fb2e3e16a5a8d542b40f796196 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sunwoong Joo <gomida@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:51:36 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] headless, media: renderer-side capture audio sinks and
 PCM in the frame stream

Patch 8 of the deterministic capture series.

- CaptureAudioDeviceFactory replaces Blink's AudioDeviceFactory in
  --deterministic-capture renderers: every media element and AudioContext
  gets a CaptureAudioRendererSink that renders only when asked. Sinks are
  registered with CaptureAudioEngine, which owns the capture audio thread and
  the device format from --deterministic-capture-audio=RATE,CHANNELS,FRAMES
  (default 48000,2,128).
- CaptureAgent.Prepare step 4: the engine renders every sink through S(n+1)
  device frames and returns the interval's float mix. Media elements are
  rendered as one request of exactly the interval's frames with no output
  delay, so AudioClock and video.currentTime read exactly T_n - start; Web
  Audio destinations render whole 128-frame quanta into a FIFO reported as
  output delay, so AudioContext.currentTime is the first quantum boundary at
  or past T_n. Mixing is a float sum in creation order with ChannelMixer and
  MultiChannelResampler for sinks whose format differs from the device.
- CaptureSession checks the count against S(n+1) - S(n), converts to the
  configured sample format (s16 or f32), hashes the interval (pcmFrameHash),
  chains pcmHash, counts audioSampleFrames and hands the bytes to the shm
  ring slot's audio area with the video frame; the ring's audio format is
  validated against the configuration. Feature audioRender is advertised.
- AudioRendererImpl: in capture mode the output uses the device rate through
  the AudioBufferConverter (no sink-side resampling), and Render() waits for
  decoded audio instead of writing silence, cancelled before the sink pauses
  or stops.
- RendererWebAudioDeviceImpl skips the SilentSinkSuspender in capture mode.

Measured on 158 with a WebM carrying Vorbis audio plus an oscillator: PCM
hashes identical across runs; a 150-frame 60000/1001 capture in three chunks
equals the serial render frame by frame for video and PCM and joins to
exactly 120120 sample frames.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
